  <h1>Pharmacodynamics: Signal Transduction, Receptors & Dose-Response</h1>
  <p>Pharmacodynamics is the study of what drugs do to the body and how they do it. It explores the molecular mechanisms of drug action, receptor interactions, signal amplification, and the mathematical relationship between drug concentration and pharmacological effect.</p>

  <!-- ANIMATED SIGNAL TRANSDUCTION -->
  <div class="animation-container">
    <h3 style="color: var(--primary-dark); margin-bottom: 10px;">⚡ Animated Signal Transduction Pathway</h3>
    <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 25px;">Track how extracellular signals trigger intracellular cellular cascades:</p>
    
    <div style="position: relative; padding-top: 20px;">
      <div class="moving-signal">⚡</div>
      <div class="pipeline">
        <div class="pipeline-step">1. Drug Binding<br><small>Receptor Activation</small></div>
        <div class="pipeline-step">2. Transduction<br><small>Second Messengers</small></div>
        <div class="pipeline-step">3. Amplification<br><small>Enzyme Cascades</small></div>
        <div class="pipeline-step">4. Cellular Response<br><small>Physiologic Effect</small></div>
